\tag{connes}
\tag{lean}
\title{Formalization motivation}

\p{The formalization asks how much of that information-loss taxonomy can
surface in explicit proof interfaces. Lean turns the claim that a factor
forgets structure into an auditable dependency map.}

\ul{
  \li{\strong{Expose hidden interfaces:} square-span, Fourier shear,
  measurable transport, continuous closure, spectral detection, characteristic
  kernels, and quotient-twisted modules.}
  \li{\strong{Separate routine translation from proof design:} the concrete
  boundaries are summarized in \ref{connes-000K}.}
  \li{\strong{Make forgetting auditable:} each change of structure crosses a
  named Lean interface.}
}

\p{\strong{Library consumer.} The project is a demanding consumer of Mathlib
and TauCeti. It reuses
their algebraic, analytic, and representation-theoretic infrastructure while
identifying interfaces that would make later formalizations less bespoke. The
present library boundary is recorded in \ref{connes-000G}.}
